<title>USA: Transcrypt to acquire EF Johnson Co.</title>
<headline>Transcrypt to acquire EF Johnson Co.</headline>
<dateline>LINCOLN, Neb. 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transcrypt International Inc said Thursday it has signed a letter of intent to acquire EF Johnson Company, a private developer and manufacturer of wireless communications products, for about $34 million.</p>
<p>EF Johnson, which is based in Waseca, Minn., had 1996 revenues of $79.3 million. Transcrypt, which designs and manufactures scrambling and encryption devices, had 1996 revenues of $13.8 million.</p>
<p>The proposed acquisition calls for total consideration of about $34 million to be paid in cash or debt assumed at closing, the company said. (-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610)</p>
</text>
